// Global serial queue for Nominatim. Their public service caps at ~1 req/sec
// per IP; firing 20+ in parallel returns 429s (which the browser surfaces
// as CORS errors because the rate-limit response lacks CORS headers).
// Single in-flight request, with a 1.1s gap after each one.
var _geoQueue = [];
var _geoQueueRunning = false;
function _runGeoQueue(){
  if (_geoQueueRunning) return;
  var task = _geoQueue.shift();
  if (!task) return;
  _geoQueueRunning = true;
  // PD.480 (network reliability): race the task against a timeout. The
  // Nominatim fetch inside the task has no timeout, so on bad signal it
  // can hang forever — the task promise never settles, _geoQueueRunning
  // stays true, and the WHOLE geo queue latches dead for the session (no
  // pin ever geocodes again). The 12s race guarantees the chain always
  // settles so the queue keeps draining; a hung fetch is just abandoned
  // (its in-flight latch clears in ensureCoarseGeocode's finally, so the
  // place is retryable later).
  Promise.race([
      Promise.resolve().then(task),
      new Promise(function(res){ setTimeout(res, 12000); })
    ])
    .catch(function(){ /* errors handled per-task */ })
    .then(function(){
      setTimeout(function(){
        _geoQueueRunning = false;
        _runGeoQueue();
      }, 1100);
    });
}
function _enqueueGeo(task){ _geoQueue.push(task); _runGeoQueue(); }

// v359.60.79: detect Nominatim result types that are "wilderness"
