    // INSTANT the user clicks "Open in discovery" (the classifier LLM
    // call runs ~10-20s before the picker even opens — that gap was a
    // dead screen), and (b) the route dispatcher can RE-CONTEXT the
    // text when the user moves to the trip view mid-build (the copy
    // was chosen once at enhance-start and went stale).
    // PD.363: the banner is a function of STATE, not event history.
    // recontext() is called on every screen change (dispatcher) and
    // picker render: if no build is running, any banner is stale by
    // definition and is removed; if one IS running, the copy is
    // re-derived from the current phase and the trip's actual shape.
    // This kills the whole class of "banner from the previous screen
    // / previous build is still up, with the wrong words."
